8. **References** - 13 references covering diabetes research, gene editing, immune evasion, and islet transplantation

The proposal addresses the novelty requirement by integrating both adaptive immunity evasion (MHC-I/II knockout via B2M/CIITA) and innate immunity evasion (CD47 overexpression for macrophage protection) in a single iPSC-derived cell therapy product specifically designed for Type 1 Diabetes - a genuinely novel dual-layer approach not previously reported.
